Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.95,0:00:09.01,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.49,0:00:31.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You're on a move!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.01,0:01:09.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Bakura, what have you done to them?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.65,0:01:12.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Answer me!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.79,0:01:18.71,Default,,0,0,0,,These two delinquents received\Nexactly what they deserved, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.11,0:01:22.17,Default,,0,0,0,,They took possession of something\Nthat didn't belong to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.25,0:01:25.03,Default,,0,0,0,,So I banished their souls\Nto the Shadow Realm.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.49,0:01:28.49,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'd say the punishment fit the crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.21,0:01:31.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You sent them to the Shadow Realm?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.61,0:01:34.32,Default,,0,0,0,,You should be showing a\Nlittle more gratitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.69,0:01:37.59,Default,,0,0,0,,After all, I've returned your belongings.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.33,0:01:42.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, most of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.31,0:01:43.31,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.27,0:01:45.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Take a look.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.71,0:01:50.09,Default,,0,0,0,,There was one item in your bag of tricks\Nthat I'm not quite ready to part with.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.17,0:01:54.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Besides, it did belong to me\Nat one time. Give it back!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.49,0:01:56.67,Default,,0,0,0,,The Millennium Items belong together!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.03,0:01:58.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Eventually, they will be.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.71,0:01:59.54,Default,,0,0,0,,In the meantime,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.62,0:02:03.76,Default,,0,0,0,,why don't you concentrate on gathering\Nthe other items instead of pestering me?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.85,0:02:07.49,Default,,0,0,0,,And when the time is right, I'll\Ngive you the Millennium Ring.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.57,0:02:11.34,Default,,0,0,0,,We may not be fond of each other,\Nbut we do share a common goal.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.65,0:02:15.51,Default,,0,0,0,,We both want all seven items\Nreturned to their resting place,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.99,0:02:18.70,Default,,0,0,0,,united once again within\Nthe Millennium Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.15,0:02:21.49,Default,,0,0,0,,just as they were so long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.99,0:02:24.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't trust you, and I never will!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.35,0:02:27.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm collecting the\NMillennium Items so I can
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.33,0:02:30.21,Default,,0,0,0,,help the Pharaoh save the\Nworld from destruction!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.79,0:02:34.32,Default,,0,0,0,,And I gather you think that I\Nhave a different goal in mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.73,0:02:36.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Believe whatever you wish,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.45,0:02:38.91,Default,,0,0,0,,but remember I know\Nthings about the past that
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.99,0:02:42.15,Default,,0,0,0,,your Pharaoh friend seems\Nto have forgotten. Oh yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.39,0:02:44.23,Default,,0,0,0,,And what kind of things are those?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.31,0:02:48.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I know that when the seven Millennium\NItems are returned to the stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.29,0:02:50.64,Default,,0,0,0,,a doorway to the Spirit World will open.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.21,0:02:52.21,Default,,0,0,0,,The spirit world?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.43,0:02:56.17,Default,,0,0,0,,If that exists, it could be where\Nthe spirit of the pharaoh belongs.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.25,0:03:00.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you saying that when this doorway\Nopens, the pharaoh will be set free?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.49,0:03:01.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You're catching on.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.17,0:03:04.25,Default,,0,0,0,,So don't you want to help your friend?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.33,0:03:08.33,Default,,0,0,0,,After all, his spirit's been trapped\Nin that puzzle for 5,000 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.67,0:03:09.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course I do!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.99,0:03:12.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Yu-Gi-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.53,0:03:15.49,Default,,0,0,0,,That's enough!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.83,0:03:17.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop poisoning Yu-Gi's mind!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.49,0:03:20.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, Pharaoh, to what do I owe this honor?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.47,0:03:25.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you come here so we can bury\Nthe hatchet and join forces?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.09,0:03:26.65,Default,,0,0,0,,You know better than that!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.91,0:03:28.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I know why you hate me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.67,0:03:30.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Because when you get right down to it,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.85,0:03:33.43,Default,,0,0,0,,you and I are more alike\Nthan you'd care to admit.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.51,0:03:35.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Isn't that right, Pharaoh?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.33,0:03:36.85,Default,,0,0,0,,We are nothing alike!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.63,0:03:40.65,Default,,0,0,0,,We're both 5,000-year-old\Nspirits, aren't we?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.91,0:03:44.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Each one inhabiting the body\Nof an innocent civilian.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.85,0:03:48.29,Default,,0,0,0,,The only difference is I remember my past.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.51,0:03:52.05,Default,,0,0,0,,All your mind contains is an\Nendless labyrinth of questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.59,0:03:55.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Your whole life is nothing more\Nthan a puzzle wrapped in a game.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.99,0:03:58.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And I happen to know the solution.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.37,0:04:00.21,Default,,0,0,0,,It's quite ironic, actually.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.57,0:04:05.33,Default,,0,0,0,,The only way you can solve\Nthat game is by playing a game.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.59,0:04:09.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know if you speak the truth,\Nbut I'll do whatever I have to.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.71,0:04:14.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Game or no game, I will unlock my mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.73,0:04:16.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Well then, best of luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.55,0:04:20.14,Default,,0,0,0,,You're going to need it when\Nthe Ultimate Shadow Game begins.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.23,0:04:22.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Enjoy your travels, Farrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.81,0:04:28.45,Default,,0,0,0,,That encounter went exactly as planned.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.91,0:04:30.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Now on to Phase 2.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.31,0:04:45.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, great.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.65,0:04:47.37,Default,,0,0,0,,The power is completely dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.21,0:04:54.27,Default,,0,0,0,,It's been quite a while, hasn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.85,0:04:56.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Can I help you with something?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.55,0:05:00.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Mogumar!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.46,0:05:02.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think he can hear you, Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.35,0:05:05.49,Default,,0,0,0,,But perhaps if you came up here\Nwith your cards and your dual disc,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.57,0:05:07.98,Default,,0,0,0,,you'd have a bit more luck communicating.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.97,0:05:09.80,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.69,0:05:18.95,Default,,0,0,0,,If that freak wants a duel, I'll\Ngive him one he'll never forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.59,0:05:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Mokuba!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.73,0:05:39.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I would tell you where his soul is,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.49,0:05:41.87,Default,,0,0,0,,but you don't believe in\Nthe Shadow Realm, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.95,0:05:44.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Whatever you did to my\Nbrother, you better undo.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.11,0:05:46.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you understand me, Bakura?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.17,0:05:49.81,Default,,0,0,0,,As soon as I defeat you, I want him back.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.03,0:05:52.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Now let's get your little game over with.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.73,0:05:54.99,Default,,0,0,0,,As you wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.31,0:05:57.31,Default,,0,0,0,,You're about to regret this.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.89,0:06:01.81,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll see.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.77,0:06:03.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.63,0:06:08.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Now for the fun part.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.47,0:06:14.39,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.73,0:06:16.97,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no such thing as magic, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.19,0:06:21.91,Default,,0,0,0,,And all those ancient visions you've been\Nhaving, they don't exist either, do they?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.99,0:06:24.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Not that Egyptian speech again.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.43,0:06:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,When are you people gonna realize\Nthat I focus on the future?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.47,0:06:31.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't waste my time\Nworrying about the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.15,0:06:38.67,Default,,0,0,0,,That attitude of yours hasn't changed\Nin over 5,000 years. That's enough!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.09,0:06:41.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Just give me a little time, Seto Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.17,0:06:44.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll make a believer out of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.51,0:06:47.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Before this shadow game comes to a close,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.33,0:06:50.03,Default,,0,0,0,,not only will you accept\Nyour ancient heritage,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.11,0:06:52.73,Default,,0,0,0,,you'll long to return to your roots.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.09,0:06:55.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Let the game commence.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.35,0:06:57.37,Default,,0,0,0,,My move.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.75,0:06:58.81,Default,,0,0,0,,First I'll play...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.83,0:07:00.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Polymerization.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.11,0:07:05.29,Default,,0,0,0,,fusing my earl and my knight\Nto form the Duke of Jemais!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.69,0:07:10.41,Default,,0,0,0,,But the rules forbid me to attack you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.69,0:07:14.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I suppose you got off easy\Nthis time, Kaiba. Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.81,0:07:19.05,Default,,0,0,0,,It'll take a lot more than a rotting\Ncarcass with a sword to intimidate me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.13,0:07:20.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Now watch how it's done!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.13,0:07:23.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I summon my Virus Raider in attack mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.09,0:07:27.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.03,0:07:32.73,Default,,0,0,0,,but it seems your monster's a few\Npoints shot I'm not done Next,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.93,0:07:36.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll activate this.\NIt's my shrink card. And
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.37,0:07:38.90,Default,,0,0,0,,it cuts your corpse's\Nattack points in half
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.71,0:07:43.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Force Raider, attack now!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.81,0:07:52.91,Default,,0,0,0,,My attack may not have\Ndestroyed your monster
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.41,0:07:56.17,Default,,0,0,0,,But it did remove 900 of your life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.57,0:07:57.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha ha ha ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.99,0:07:59.73,Default,,0,0,0,,And you think that worries me?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.81,0:08:02.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't be laughing if I were you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.51,0:08:03.61,Default,,0,0,0,,And why is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.23,0:08:05.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, for one,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.45,0:08:09.29,Default,,0,0,0,,you're about to lose another 500 of\Nyour life points thanks to your friend,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.37,0:08:10.53,Default,,0,0,0,,the Duke of Demise.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.83,0:08:12.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that reason enough for you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.01,0:08:16.31,Default,,0,0,0,,No, because I have something\Nfar worse in store.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.95,0:08:22.47,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I'll sacrifice my Duke in\Norder to summon my dear bound colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.91,0:08:25.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I activate the magic\Ncard Spirit Illusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.17,0:08:28.64,Default,,0,0,0,,It creates what's known as a doppelganger,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.85,0:08:33.44,Default,,0,0,0,,an exact duplicate of my monster, complete\Nwith all the power of the original.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.79,0:08:35.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.83,0:08:38.15,Default,,0,0,0,,So now you've got two useless monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.07,0:08:40.81,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll see about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.29,0:08:43.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, doppelganger, diavau!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.33,0:08:48.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Did I forget to mention my\Ndoppelganger's special ability?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.43,0:08:50.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Whenever it strikes,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.07,0:08:55.84,Default,,0,0,0,,your monster automatically loses attack\Npoints equal to those of my doppelganger.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.21,0:09:02.11,Default,,0,0,0,,That leaves your Voseraider in\Nquite a compromising position.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.41,0:09:07.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, dearbound colonel, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.23,0:09:15.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, I'll place this face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.79,0:09:16.87,Default,,0,0,0,,That ends my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.95,0:09:19.01,Default,,0,0,0,,No more Mr. Nice Guy!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.29,0:09:20.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I play this!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.79,0:09:22.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Lord of Dragons!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.95,0:09:25.65,Default,,0,0,0,,It's just as I planned.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.19,0:09:29.19,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as my Lord of\NDragons is on the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.39,0:09:32.68,Default,,0,0,0,,any dragon I play is safe\Nfrom all magic and trap cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.97,0:09:36.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Therefore, I activate the\NFlute of Summoning Dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.35,0:09:40.82,Default,,0,0,0,,When both of these cards are on the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.01,0:09:43.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I can summon any two dragons from my hand!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.29,0:09:47.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Excellent
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.59,0:09:48.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Actually,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.63,0:09:49.91,Default,,0,0,0,,now that I think of it,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.99,0:09:54.57,Default,,0,0,0,,there's only one dragon that I\Nneed My blue-eyes, white dragon
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.05,0:09:59.53,Default,,0,0,0,,That's just the card I\Nhoped you'd play. Now
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.61,0:10:02.32,Default,,0,0,0,,it's time for a little\Nstroll down memory lane
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.07,0:10:07.47,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.17,0:10:14.31,Default,,0,0,0,,What has he done to you, Kisara?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.67,0:10:20.15,Default,,0,0,0,,In the name of the\Npharaoh, I will save thee
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.87,0:10:24.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh no!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.25,0:10:26.65,Default,,0,0,0,,It's that vision again!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.37,0:10:40.37,Default,,0,0,0,,My mind's playing tricks on me again.\NJust like when I dueled against Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.05,0:10:45.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Neither of our god cards\Nwill give up. You're
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.27,0:10:47.99,Default,,0,0,0,,right It must be a holographic malfunction
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.41,0:11:07.29,Default,,0,0,0,,This can't be real!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.99,0:11:17.23,Default,,0,0,0,,My Millennium Puzzle\Ntransported us to another place.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.69,0:11:20.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps another time. What? But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.55,0:11:23.90,Default,,0,0,0,,This has to be some kind of an illusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.05,0:11:26.23,Default,,0,0,0,,We were just in the middle of a duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.49,0:11:32.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Something about this place\Nseems familiar to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.87,0:11:35.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Could it be possible that\Nwe're in ancient Egypt?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.15,0:11:44.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not falling for that nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.75,0:11:48.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Whatever happened in the past\Nhas nothing to do with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.75,0:11:50.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Kaiba, something wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.73,0:11:52.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you feeling all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.03,0:12:01.43,Default,,0,0,0,,i've never felt better now let's get back\Nto the duel shall we all right blue eyes
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.51,0:12:04.57,Default,,0,0,0,,destroy his dear bound white lightning
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.65,0:12:10.11,Default,,0,0,0,,attack not so fast i\Nactivate my spirit shield
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.29,0:12:16.39,Default,,0,0,0,,no way i'm afraid so thanks to my shield
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.47,0:12:18.49,Default,,0,0,0,,your attack didn't get\Nanywhere near my dear
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.57,0:12:21.75,Default,,0,0,0,,bound And all I had to do was extract one
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.83,0:12:24.99,Default,,0,0,0,,monster from my graveyard\Nand remove it from play.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.41,0:12:28.91,Default,,0,0,0,,So as long as I can keep a fresh\Nsupply of creatures in my graveyard,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.99,0:12:30.46,Default,,0,0,0,,your attacks are useless.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.61,0:12:33.75,Default,,0,0,0,,In simpler terms, my life\Npoints are untouchable.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.11,0:12:35.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, maybe for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.53,0:12:36.91,Default,,0,0,0,,But that won't last.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.13,0:12:40.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I place one card face\Ndown and end my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.61,0:12:45.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Soon the power of Kaiba's Blue-Eyes\NWhite Dragon will rest in my hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.99,0:12:49.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll begin my turn by\Nactivating the magic card,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.11,0:12:54.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Part of Greed. That allows\Nme to draw two more cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.21,0:12:58.07,Default,,0,0,0,,from my deck And one of them\Nhappens to be Greed Tablet
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.19,0:13:04.97,Default,,0,0,0,,What'd you do to my monster?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.03,0:13:09.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Lord of Dragons, along\Nwith all of its powers,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.99,0:13:13.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Has been sealed away in that\Nstone tablet, and there's
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.47,0:13:16.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Only one way to set it free:\Nyou must shatter the stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.99,0:13:20.57,Default,,0,0,0,,however once my grief tablet\Nis destroyed you'll receive
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.65,0:13:26.71,Default,,0,0,0,,500 points of damage now my\Ndoppelganger weaken his dragon
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.59,0:13:36.55,Default,,0,0,0,,my blue eyes all righty about attack
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.87,0:13:41.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate Attack Guidance Armor!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.61,0:13:50.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.52,0:13:51.68,Default,,0,0,0,,You're safe for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.91,0:13:55.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll end my turn by placing two\Ncards face down on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.89,0:13:57.39,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all over for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.47,0:14:01.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I can sense your fear, Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.13,0:14:06.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You're gonna pay for what\Nyou did to Mokuba, you rat.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.55,0:14:09.96,Default,,0,0,0,,No one messes with the Kaiba\Nfamily and gets away with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.09,0:14:13.97,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time to turn this duel\Naround by playing Card of Demise.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.41,0:14:16.45,Default,,0,0,0,,It lets me draw four cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.73,0:14:19.79,Default,,0,0,0,,And after five turns, my\Nhand goes to the graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.69,0:14:23.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you forgetting about my spirit shield?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.99,0:14:26.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing you draw can damage me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.55,0:14:28.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid I'm gonna have to disagree.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.41,0:14:31.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I activate Soul Release.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.61,0:14:33.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what that means, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.65,0:14:36.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I can remove up to five\Ncards from your graveyard,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.95,0:14:40.35,Default,,0,0,0,,and without your monsters\Nto fuel its power,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.59,0:14:42.47,Default,,0,0,0,,your spirit shield is destroyed!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.69,0:14:51.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, I'll use Silent Doom to bring\Nback a monster in defense mode,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.19,0:14:54.37,Default,,0,0,0,,and I choose Force Raider!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.99,0:14:59.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'll sacrifice Force\NRaider and my blue eyes!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.93,0:15:03.22,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the only way I can get\Nmy dragon's strength back!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.45,0:15:08.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Blue-Eyes White Dragon, return!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.87,0:15:11.27,Default,,0,0,0,,So what's your point?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.49,0:15:15.55,Default,,0,0,0,,The mighty Blue-Eyes has been reborn\Nand I'm supposed to run in fear?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.69,0:15:19.69,Default,,0,0,0,,You will when he attacks your little\Nsnake boy with white lightning!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.03,0:15:30.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Not bad, but not good\Nenough to defeat me, Kaiba!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.21,0:15:36.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate my mirror tablet trap card,\Nthen I activate my rebirth tablet,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.63,0:15:39.09,Default,,0,0,0,,so say hello to an old friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.59,0:15:43.42,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.87,0:15:48.21,Default,,0,0,0,,My rebirth tablet was activated as\Nsoon as my Deerbound was destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.69,0:15:52.16,Default,,0,0,0,,That allowed me to immediately\Nbring him back to the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.55,0:15:54.85,Default,,0,0,0,,But wait, there's more.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.87,0:16:04.03,Default,,0,0,0,,After you sacrificed your\Nblue-eyes white dragon,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.49,0:16:08.05,Default,,0,0,0,,my mirror tablet was able to\Nabsorb half its attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.33,0:16:11.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Then they were graciously\Ndonated to my Deerbound,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.67,0:16:14.71,Default,,0,0,0,,making him the strongest\Nmonster on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.37,0:16:18.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Say farewell to your blue-eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.07,0:16:21.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Deerbound, destroy him now!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.03,0:16:29.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, but no dice.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.21,0:16:32.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate Monster Reborn!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.37,0:16:36.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Blue Eyes is back!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.07,0:16:40.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, if he only knew what my\NDiabound has just accomplished.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.45,0:16:46.75,Default,,0,0,0,,By destroying his Blue Eyes, it was able\Nto duplicate and absorb its attack power.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.23,0:16:49.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd say mission accomplished.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.29,0:16:56.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh well, I guess you're in luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.09,0:17:01.61,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, Kaiba, I have some other\Nbusiness to attend to. You're joking!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.91,0:17:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You're leaving in the middle of a duel?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.17,0:17:07.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Trust me, I'll return soon enough\Nto finish what I've started.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.91,0:17:09.51,Default,,0,0,0,,In the meantime, take this.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.95,0:17:12.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.97,0:17:14.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Didn't this belong to Pegasus?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.15,0:17:17.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Why, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.53,0:17:20.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe he once used\Nit to capture your soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.15,0:17:26.61,Default,,0,0,0,,The Millennium Eye
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.65,0:17:28.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Excellent memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.85,0:17:30.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Kaiba It's a wonder you don't remember
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.99,0:17:33.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Anything about your ancient\Npast? I'll tell you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.93,0:17:36.67,Default,,0,0,0,,what Bring the Millennium Eye to Egypt And
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.75,0:17:39.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll give you a little\Nhistory lesson Sorry,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.31,0:17:41.47,Default,,0,0,0,,but I don't have time to\Nrun halfway around the
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.55,0:17:44.67,Default,,0,0,0,,world chasing a fairy tale\NI have a company to run,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.81,0:17:45.64,Default,,0,0,0,,remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.72,0:17:47.38,Default,,0,0,0,,So you're not interested\Nin learning why you
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.47,0:17:50.12,Default,,0,0,0,,share such a strong bond\Nwith your blue eyes?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.45,0:17:52.39,Default,,0,0,0,,And what's that supposed to mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.75,0:17:55.93,Default,,0,0,0,,The answer lies in the\Nsands of Egypt. Seto!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.43,0:18:15.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Like I'm going to Egypt because\Nsome lunatic told me to.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.11,0:18:34.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Attention passengers, flight 706 flying\Nnon-stop to Cairo, Egypt, is now boarding.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.29,0:18:39.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, what are you guys doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.37,0:18:43.75,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you think, Yug?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.95,0:18:46.36,Default,,0,0,0,,We're all coming to Egypt with you, dude.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.61,0:18:48.14,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't have to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.27,0:18:49.10,Default,,0,0,0,,You kidding?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.18,0:18:50.36,Default,,0,0,0,,We would miss this for the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.45,0:18:52.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And besides, Taya paid for the tickets.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.53,0:18:56.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Try I lent you the money, because you\Ntwo conveniently forgot your wallets.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.21,0:18:58.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Right, that's what I meant.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.81,0:19:01.87,Default,,0,0,0,,And Tristan and I are going\Nto pay back every penny.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.11,0:19:04.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, in fact, my check's\Nin the mail already.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.15,0:19:09.23,Default,,0,0,0,,The important thing is we're not\Nletting you take this trip alone, pal.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.31,0:19:12.79,Default,,0,0,0,,We know how much this means to\Nyou, and we wouldn't miss it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.87,0:19:13.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.01,0:19:15.69,Default,,0,0,0,,You guys are the best.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.97,0:19:17.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, what are we waiting for?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.49,0:19:18.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go. Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.71,0:19:23.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope we're ready for this, Yugi,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.13,0:19:27.31,Default,,0,0,0,,for it's so much more than\Njust a trip to my homeland.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.47,0:19:31.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a journey into my ancient past.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.67,0:19:40.44,Default,,0,0,0,,On behalf of the flight crew, I'd like to\Nwelcome you aboard flight 706 to Cairo.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.31,0:19:46.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Pharaoh, I hope you find\Nwhat you're looking for.
